# ── SPEC-0200 rule 4 + rule 7 — the LIVE switch (T-12182, plan card C3) ──────────────────────────
#
# WHAT THIS BLOCK IS. C1 taught the parser the response contract, C2 built the decision core and C4
# built the instrumentation — and NONE of it was reachable from a live run. This block plus the
# `_consult_adjudicate` wiring below is the switch that makes all three live AT ONCE, because
# SPEC-0200 rule 7 says so in as many words: «Prompt and predicates change TOGETHER — a partially
# landed state is not a valid state of this contract». A prompt overlay without the re-keyed
# predicates would ask the auditor for a delta and then judge the answer by the whole-subject rules;
# predicates without the persisted option pair would compare a survivor against a reconstruction.
# Either half alone is a CONTRADICTORY interim state, which is why the atom is the commit.
#
# WHY THE SWITCH IS AT THE ENGINE AND NOT AT THE PRODUCERS. `_consult_adjudicate` is the ONE consult
# engine both producers already call (`cmd_audit`'s dispatched-worker auto-consult and the
# `audit consult` verb, the latter also serving the plan-gate target through `bin/lib/plan.py`). Rule
# 9 states the consequence rather than asking for it: «this contract binds the engine, so both
# producers comply by construction». Editing three prompt builders instead would be three places for
# the delta contract to drift apart, and the AC5 producer-parity e2e exists precisely to prove they
# do not.

#: SPEC-0200 rule 2 / rule 10 — the exhaustive-survey directive, RE-HOMED TO ROUND 0 ONLY.
#: Restored from the T-12141 original (commit 894f3fd663, withdrawn whole by T-12168) with ONE
#: deliberate departure, called out because a silent one would read as a transcription slip: the
#: original promised «you will be asked ONCE for the rest in this same pass», and SPEC-0200 rule 3
#: RETIRES that re-ask in as many words — «there is NO re-ask (every auditor invocation is RECORDED
#: as a round)». Rule 2 also demotes the declaration from a gate to a RECORDED fact: a missing or
#: `false` declaration freezes exactly what was returned and records violation `incomplete-survey`.
#: So the two sentences that described the retired mechanism are replaced by what actually happens
#: now. Everything else is the original text.
#:
#: The clause rides ROUND 0 and nowhere else. That is the whole retirement of rule 10's second item
#: («the whole-subject re-survey inside a retest»): under T-12141 this text rode EVERY prompt from
#: one home, which is what ordered a fresh whole-subject survey on every pass and drove audit-post
#: RED share 16% -> 44% and max consult rounds per (task, stage) 1 -> 11.
#: T-12288 (SPEC-0204 rule 8) — ONE BODY, TWO FRAMES. Rule 8 moves the round-0-only survey directive
#: BELOW the ceiling, where the "round 0 of this ceiling episode" framing above is simply untrue: an
#: ordinary pass 1 of `audit pre|post` is not a round of any episode. The two clauses differ ONLY in
#: that opening frame, so the frame is a parameter and the BODY — every rule about what a complete
#: survey is — is shared. Copying the body under a second name is what would let the below-ceiling
#: and above-ceiling surveys drift into two different asks (CHARTER §P5), which is exactly the
#: divergence rule 8's "no new mechanism" forbids.
_CONSULT_ROUND0_FRAME = (
    "## Full verdict — enumerate EVERY defect, never one per round (SPEC-0200 rule 2)\n\n"
    "This is the BASELINE round (round 0) of this ceiling episode, and it is the ONLY round that\n"
    "surveys the whole subject. Your survey is FROZEN as this card's defect baseline; every later\n"
    "round judges ONLY the ids you name here. A defect you omit now does not get a later round to\n"
    "surface in — it becomes a measured COMPLETENESS FAILURE against this survey.\n"
)
#: The BELOW-CEILING frame (SPEC-0204 rule 8): pass 1 of an ordinary audit-pre/post is the ONE pass
#: that surveys the whole subject; every later pass judges the delta. A defect omitted here is not
#: lost — rule 8 lets a later pass raise it as a `pre-existing-in-subject` LATE FINDING, which is
#: RECORDED and must be decided but never drives that pass's verdict (owner ruling D8: the auditor's
#: completeness is recorded, never a gate). Saying so is what makes an honest late finding cost the
#: auditor nothing, which is the only reason to expect one.
_BASE_PASS1_FRAME = (
    "## Full verdict — enumerate EVERY defect, never one per pass (SPEC-0204 rule 8)\n\n"
    "This is PASS 1 of this audit stage, and it is the ONLY pass that surveys the whole subject.\n"
    "Every later pass judges the closure of what you name here plus any regression the change\n"
    "introduces — it does NOT re-survey. A defect you omit now can still be raised on a later pass as\n"
    "`causality: pre-existing-in-subject`, where it is RECORDED as a late finding and must be decided\n"
    "before the card closes, but never drives that pass's verdict. So name every defect you can see\n"
    "NOW; and if you see one later, say plainly that it was pre-existing — it costs this change\n"
    "nothing and hiding it costs the session a pass.\n"
)


def _full_verdict_clause(frame: str) -> str:
    """The exhaustive-survey directive under `frame` — the shared BODY, one framing sentence apart.

    Pure f(frame). The consult constant below is this function applied to the round-0 frame and is
    BYTE-IDENTICAL to the text that shipped before T-12288, so the consult prompt is unchanged; the
    below-ceiling pass-1 clause is the same body under `_BASE_PASS1_FRAME`."""
    return (
        frame
        + "- A BLOCKING outcome MUST enumerate the COMPLETE set of defects you would block on over the\n"
        "  WHOLE subject — every one, each with a LOCATOR (file:line or scope ref) and the FAILING\n"
        "  INPUT that demonstrates it. Naming one defect and stopping is an INCOMPLETE verdict, not a\n"
        "  short one: it costs the session a full rework-and-re-audit round per defect, which is the\n"
        "  exact waste this rule removes. Survey the whole subject FIRST, then report.\n"
        "- A HOLD survivor MUST rest on that SAME exhaustive list. A HOLD that names one defect while\n"
        "  you can see others is NON-CONVERGED BY CONSTRUCTION — list them all under `findings:` so\n"
        "  the session can resolve them in ONE pass.\n"
        "- Declare `findings_complete: true | false` in your output YAML. `true` means: you surveyed\n"
        "  the whole subject and this list is exhaustive. `false` means a remainder exists — say so\n"
        "  plainly. The declaration is RECORDED, never a gate: a missing or `false` declaration freezes\n"
        "  exactly what you returned and records the fact. There is NO follow-up ask — every auditor\n"
        "  invocation is a counted round, so this survey is the one you get.\n"
        "This does NOT lower the bar for what counts as a defect, and does NOT ask you to pad the list:\n"
        "report every REAL defect you would block on, and no invented ones. Completeness, not volume.\n"
    )


_AUDIT_FULL_VERDICT_CLAUSE = _full_verdict_clause(_CONSULT_ROUND0_FRAME)
#: SPEC-0204 rule 8 — the PASS-1-ONLY survey directive of an ordinary (below-ceiling) TASK
#: audit-pre/post. Appended by `build_audit_prompt` exactly when the pass-N>=2 monotonic section did
